{"step_index":390,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T21:06:27Z","content":"Now, let's build the **Actual Sovra-Native Compiler Front-End and Code Generator** (`ops/runtime/sovrac.zig`) in native Zig!\n\nLet's design `sovrac.zig` to meet all 5 requirements:\n1. **Lexer**: Tokenizes `.sovra` source text into keywords (`fn`, `candidate`, `decision`, `gate`, `struct`, `@invariant`, `SHM_RingBuffer`, `HyperVector`), identifiers, operators, and literals.\n2. **Parser**: Parses tokens into a strongly-typed Abstract Syntax Tree (`AstNode`: `VarDecl`, `TypeSpec`, `GateBlock`, `InvariantDecl`, `CallExpr`).\n3. **Type Checker (`typecheck()`)**:\n   - Tracks variable types (`CandidateType`, `DecisionType`, `PrimitiveType`).\n   - If an assignment `val y: decision<T> = x;` is encountered where `x` is `candidate<T>` and HAS NOT passed through `gate(...)`, the compiler raises a **HARD TYPE CHECKING ERROR**:\n     `[SOVRA-COMPILER ERROR] Line 14: Invalid type coercion! Cannot assign raw 'candidate<ToolCall>' to 'decision<ToolCall>' without wrapping in a certified 'gate(...)' block.`\n   - Rejects the compilation immediately with exit code 1!\n4. **AST Invariant Verifier (`verify_invariants()`)**:\n   - Audits `@invariant(...)` declarations against the function body. If a function contains `@invariant(truth)` but lacks verification assertions, it raises a **HARD INVARIANT COMPILER ERROR**:\n     `[SOVRA-COMPILER ERROR] Line 22: Function 'unsafe_exec' declares @invariant(truth) but missing required empirical verification check!`\n5. **Code Generator & Native Binary Runner (`codegen()`)**:\n   - Generates and executes native C++/machine code instructions, outputting `\"Hello from Sovra Native Compiler v1.0\"`, running real native gate logic, and printing certified execution status!\n\nLet's write `ops/runtime/sovrac.zig`!","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"// SOVRA NATIVE COMPILER & AST TYPE CHECKER (sovrac.zig v1.0)\\n// Canonical Reference: Codified 2026-09-28 by Anthony & Maxx.\\n// Mission: Real Lexer, AST Parser, Type Checker, Invariant Verifier, and Code Generator for .sovra files.\\n\\nconst std = @import(\\\"std\\\");\\nconst print = std.debug.print;\\n\\npub const TokenType = enum {\\n    KwFn,\\n    KwVal,\\n    KwCandidate,\\n    KwDecision,\\n    KwGate,\\n    KwInvariant,\\n    KwShmRingBuffer,\\n    KwHyperVector,\\n    Identifier,\\n    Equals,\\n    Colon,\\n    LParen,\\n    RParen,\\n    LBrace,\\n    RBrace,\\n    LAngle,\\n    RAngle,\\n    StringLit,\\n    NumberLit,\\n    Semicolon,\\n    Eof,\\n    Invalid,\\n};\\n\\npub const Token = struct {\\n    kind: TokenType,\\n    text: []const u8,\\n    line: usize,\\n};\\n\\npub const Lexer = struct {\\n    source: []const u8,\\n    cursor: usize,\\n    line: usize,\\n\\n    pub fn init(source: []const u8) Lexer {\\n        return Lexer{\\n            .source = source,\\n            .cursor = 0,\\n            .line = 1,\\n        };\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn next_token(self: *Lexer) Token {\\n        while (self.cursor < self.source.len) {\\n            const c = self.source[self.cursor];\\n            if (c == '\\\\n') {\\n                self.line += 1;\\n                self.cursor += 1;\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            if (c == ' ' or c == '\\\\t' or c == '\\\\r') {\\n                self.cursor += 1;\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            if (c == '=' and self.cursor + 1 < self.source.len and self.source[self.cursor + 1] == '=') {\\n                self.cursor += 2;\\n                return Token{ .kind = .Equals, .text = \\\"==\\\", .line = self.line };\\n            }\\n            if (c == '=') {\\n                self.cursor += 1;\\n                return Token{ .kind = .Equals, .text = \\\"=\\\", .line = self.line };\\n            }\\n            if (c == ':') {\\n                self.cursor += 1;\\n                return Token{ .kind = .Colon, .text =